  "note": "Election of the Newcastle Urban Council, polled Wednesday 17 May 1967. Eleven nominations for nine seats. Richard James Hall, an independent, topped the poll. The News-Letter (18 May 1967, p. 2) lists the nine elected with their votes only; the Belfast Telegraph's round-up of the same day (p. 9) also names the two defeated, G. R. Peattie and John B. Hodgkins, with their votes.",
